From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:54:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the list buffer's assert-only child size only when asserts are on

VectorListBuffer::Verify() reads the child size into a local that only
D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to
nothing, -Wunused-variable reports it. The guard keeps the local to
the builds that assert; upstream later drops the local, as the size
becomes a member of the buffer.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/common/vector/list_vector.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/common/vector/list_vector.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/common/vector/list_vector.cpp
index fa2055397d..89595b6c8a 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/common/vector/list_vector.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/common/vector/list_vector.cpp
@@ -119,7 +119,9 @@ void VectorListBuffer::Verify(const LogicalType &type, const SelectionVector &se
 	// NOTE: size > capacity can occur in valid intermediate states (e.g. after SetListSize before Reserve)
 	// D_ASSERT(size <= capacity);
 	idx_t total_size = 0;
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 	auto child_size = GetSize();
+#endif
 	auto list_data = reinterpret_cast<list_entry_t *>(data_ptr);
 	for (idx_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
 		auto idx = sel.get_index(i);
